---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Brief = `We are putting photos on a device with not much room on it.
Before I buy anything I want to know how big an image
actually is, and how much I save if I drop the color
quality. Give me numbers I can read.`;

const SampleOutput = `64x64:  8-bit 12.3 kB   2-bit 3.1 kB
800x600:  8-bit 1.4 MB   2-bit 360.0 kB
4000x3000:  8-bit 36.0 MB   2-bit 9.0 MB`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/unit-2/cc-set-7" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back to Set 7
        </a>

        <h1>Code Challenge: Storage Estimate</h1>

        <h4>
          Difficulty&nbsp;&nbsp;
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
        </h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="brief">
          <h2>The Brief</h2>

          <Code code={Brief} frame="code" lang="txt" title="What they asked for" showLineNumbers={false} class="mt-3" />

          <p class="mt-4">
            <b>Write your requirements list before you write any code.</b> Input,
            calculate, output, and anything you had to decide for yourself. See{" "}
            <a href="/courses/ap-csp/unit-2/cc-set-7">Set 7</a> for what that looks like.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="notes">
          <h2>Notes</h2>

          <ul>
            <li>Three channels per pixel. The bits per channel is the thing that varies, so it is a <b>parameter</b>.</li>
            <li>Eight bits to a byte. Report bytes, not bits &mdash; nobody buys storage in bits.</li>
            <li><b>Numbers a person can read</b> is a stated requirement. 36000000 is not an answer; 36.0 MB is.</li>
            <li>Run it at three sizes that are far apart, and at two bit depths, so the saving is visible.</li>
            <li>Ignore compression entirely. Say so in your requirements list &mdash; this is the uncompressed size, which is the honest worst case.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="sample-output">
          <h2>Sample Output</h2>

          <Code code={SampleOutput} frame="terminal" title="Sample Output" lang="txt" showLineNumbers={false} class="mt-3" />

          <p class="mt-3">
            <b>Dropping from 8 bits to 2 divides the size by exactly four</b>, at every
            size. Your requirements list should predict that before you run it.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Your requirements list and your program file, named{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-theme">cc-storage-estimate</b>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <h1 class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash">
          Commence Challenge
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
